  title: Classified Research Program
  key: 11
  topic: 1
  boardContentText: 'A classified research program was established


    Additional
    equipment was installed across the island '
  boardSprite: {fileID: 0}
  contentText: "[CLASSIFIED \u2014 JOINT PROJECT AUTHORIZATION]\n\nPROJECT: SILENT
    SIGNAL (working title)\nSPONSORS: Vibration Society / Army\nACCESS LEVEL: 3\n\nI.
    OBJECTIVE\nThe joint program is established for the purpose of mapping vibrational
    and atmospheric patterns in the waters surrounding the island. The region has,
    over decades, exhibited recurring maritime anomalies \u2014 particularly fog
    formation, tidal variability, and unexplained navigational disturbances.\n\nII.
    INTENDED OUTCOMES\n- Develop a predictive model of fog and tidal behavior\n-
    Identify the causes of historical maritime incidents\n- Improve civilian and
    military navigation through the region\n- Test sub-surface vibrational sensing
    as an oceanographic tool\n\nIII. INSTALLATIONS\nThe program permits the construction
    and installation of supplementary equipment across the island, including but
    not limited to:\n- Signal redirection towers (multiple)\n- Power and generator
    network\n- Spectral and resonance instruments\n- Modifications to the existing
    lighthouse apparatus\n\nIV. CONFIDENTIALITY\nThe work shall remain confidential.
    Publication is prohibited. Public access to the island is restricted during operational
    periods.\n\nV. RESPONSIBLE PERSON\nDr. H. Vogel, Vibration Society.\nRenowned
    scientific figure. Exceptional results in the field of vibrational research.
    Following a recent personal loss (brother), exhibits signs of emotional instability;
    nevertheless, in light of past achievements, confirmed as project lead.\n\nSignature:\n[two
    illegible signatures]"
  paperSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cea3c49c6ad23de4286197f5004fc48e, type: 3}
